<spell-notebook "toast theming">
	<header level="1">
		Toast
		<header>A toast allows users to receive a short, non-blocking notification.</>
	</>
	<toast-tab-bar showing="theming"/>
	<section>
		<html>
			<ui-menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
				<ui-item link="#tokens">Tokens</>
				<ui-item link="#themes">Themes</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- THEMING:  the family's tokens, live, plus how to set them and which themes touch it. -->
	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			Theme with the public `--ui-toast-*` tokens: set one on the element, on any ancestor (`:root` for
			every toast), or on the box through `::part(box)`. They inherit into the shadow root, where the
			sheet reads each through a private alias. Never set the `--_ui-toast-*` names: they're the sheet's
			private plumbing.

			- `--ui-toast-width` applies on screens wider than a phone; phones (up to 420px) use
			  `--ui-toast-mobile-width`.
			- `--ui-toast-container-distance` goes on `:root`: the containers are page-level. For
			  `UI.toast()`'s toasts, set the rest on `:root` too.
			- Style the pieces with `::part()`: `box` (around the toast, its bar and attached actions),
			  `toast`, `icon`, `content`, `header`, `message`, `close`, `actions`, `progress` and `bar`.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```css
			:root {
			  --ui-toast-radius: 0.75em;
			}
			ui-toast::part(bar) {
			  background: var(--ui-primary);
			}
			```
		</>
		<markdown>Edit a value below to try it.</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-toast" playground>
				<ui-toast message="I am a toast, nice to meet you!"></>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>
			Each theme of the set (Spell, Glass, Fruity, Merlot, Paper, Midnight, Crisp, Pop, Matrix) changes the page, and the colours a toast takes
			from it.
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
